1
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:05,130
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:10,800
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,610 --> 00:00:14,770
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:17,650
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:21,750
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:30,560
In my eyes, a true friend is someone
who never clings to another's dream.

7
00:00:31,330 --> 00:00:33,320
Someone independent...

8
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:37,390
...who can find his own reason to live
and follow that path without guidance.

9
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:44,770
And if anyone tries to crush his
dream, protect it heart and soul.

10
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:48,800
Even if that person happened to be me.

11
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:53,050
For me, a true friend...

12
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:57,550
...is someone whom I consider my equal.

13
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:21,510
Feel no shame about shape

14
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,430
Weather changes their phrase

15
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:27,190
Even mother will show you another way

16
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:29,560
So put your glasses on

17
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:31,650
Nothing will be wrong

18
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:33,860
There's no blame. There's no fame

19
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:35,690
It's up to you

20
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:39,320
The first words should be found

21
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:42,950
Whatever holds you back

22
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:44,330
I...

23
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:45,450
...can...

24
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,620
I can get it off

25
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,620
Tell me what...

26
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:49,630
Tell me what...

27
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:51,460
Tell me what you want

28
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:52,550
I don't know why...

29
00:01:52,750 --> 00:01:53,550
Don't know why...

30
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:55,550
Don't know why you're afraid

31
00:01:55,710 --> 00:01:56,720
Tell me what...

32
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:57,680
Tell me what...

33
00:01:57,840 --> 00:01:59,340
Tell me what you'd say

34
00:01:59,590 --> 00:02:00,680
I don't know why...

35
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,760
Don't know why...

36
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:02,560
Too late...

37
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:04,180
It's too late

38
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:13,110
The Battle

39
00:02:37,130 --> 00:02:37,550
Griffi...

40
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:38,920
Sir Griffith!

41
00:02:43,970 --> 00:02:46,560
Princess Charlotte,
what has happened?

42
00:02:51,650 --> 00:02:53,980
Please, take this...

43
00:02:57,650 --> 00:03:00,360
This is a necklace made from lodestone.

44
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:04,490
It isn't anything extravagant,
but it belonged to the former queen.

45
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:06,910
It was my mother's keepsake.

46
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:08,870
Such a precious article of yours...

47
00:03:09,460 --> 00:03:10,710
I cannot accept it.

48
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,420
Please, carry this with you.

49
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:20,260
There are two of these lodestone,
a male one and a female one.

50
00:03:20,670 --> 00:03:23,720
And each attracts the other.

51
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:28,390
It's said those who hold companion
stones will always be reunited.

52
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:33,350
If you would bear this male
stone formed into a necklace...

53
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:37,610
...it may be attracted
to my female stone necklace.

54
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:41,570
And thus, you ought to return
safely from the battlefield.

55
00:03:43,530 --> 00:03:45,820
Please, I would like you to have this.

56
00:03:47,330 --> 00:03:47,950
No...

57
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:52,460
This is a precious keepsake of yours, Princess.

58
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:54,670
I cannot keep this as my possession.

59
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,090
But...

60
00:03:58,630 --> 00:04:04,470
Therefore, I will return this safely
to you as soon as I return from battle.

61
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:14,270
Honestly, never before has
the war filled me with such fear.

62
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,940
Sir Griffith, please...

63
00:04:18,650 --> 00:04:20,230
Please stay safe.

64
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:30,290
Knight, please come forward.

65
00:04:30,870 --> 00:04:32,200
Y-Yes, ma'am...

66
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:35,120
Please guard Sir Griffith well during this battle.

67
00:04:37,130 --> 00:04:39,550
Certainly, ma'am, on my life.

68
00:04:44,300 --> 00:04:45,130
Let's go.

69
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:47,260
All right...

70
00:05:02,030 --> 00:05:02,990
Charlotte.

71
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:06,280
M-Mother.

72
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:09,240
What do you think you are doing, Charlotte?

73
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,200
What do you mean?

74
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:13,660
Do not feign ignorance.

75
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:15,620
You gave that man of lesser stature a present.

76
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:19,960
It is not your concern who
I choose to give my property to!

77
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:21,090
That is improper!

78
00:05:22,090 --> 00:05:24,630
You are a member of the royal house.

79
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:29,010
To think that you gave a present
to someone of such humble origins!

80
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:32,350
When you talk to that man, concern
yourself with what others might think.

81
00:05:32,350 --> 00:05:34,850
You shall be mindful of your class.

82
00:05:35,810 --> 00:05:37,020
But, Mother...

83
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:40,900
You have turned sixteen.
You are no longer a child.

84
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:46,780
Charlotte!

85
00:06:05,130 --> 00:06:07,090
Look how popular we are!

86
00:06:07,090 --> 00:06:11,600
We are taking on the vanguard
position. It's a big responsibility.

87
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,760
Hey, are you nervous?

88
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,520
Nope!

89
00:06:14,850 --> 00:06:16,680
You seem to have lost your nerve.

90
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,890
You're shaking.

91
00:06:18,890 --> 00:06:19,850
Shut up!

92
00:06:19,850 --> 00:06:21,520
I am just excited about the whole thing!

93
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:25,190
Why is Griffith so late anyway...

94
00:06:58,930 --> 00:07:00,100
March!

95
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:37,140
For me, a true friend...

96
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:40,770
...is someone whom I consider my equal.

97
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:32,820
Oh no, why now?

98
00:08:33,450 --> 00:08:34,820
What's wrong?

99
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:36,370
You look pale.

100
00:08:36,870 --> 00:08:37,990
It's nothing.

101
00:08:37,990 --> 00:08:40,370
All right, the battle is about to begin!

102
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:52,630
Charge!

103
00:08:53,630 --> 00:08:55,430
Charge!

104
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,260
This is not going to be easy!

105
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:29,600
It's you...

106
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:32,810
...the Band of the Hawk's
sole female company commander.

107
00:10:33,190 --> 00:10:34,400
So what?

108
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:36,740
I do not like it...

109
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:39,240
...a mere woman such as you acting like a knight.

110
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:44,790
Women are inferior to men in strength,
so what use are they in killing?

111
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:46,370
If you think so, then come try me.

112
00:10:49,120 --> 00:10:50,670
What's so funny?

113
00:10:50,670 --> 00:10:55,300
I assume that you comfort your
fellow soldiers during the night...

114
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:56,550
What did you say?

115
00:10:56,550 --> 00:11:01,760
So, due to getting into Griffith's bed,
you must have won your rank...

116
00:11:01,760 --> 00:11:03,760
...as a company commander!

117
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:08,350
I would like to experience the charm
that you've used on such men.

118
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,650
You bastard!

119
00:11:16,690 --> 00:11:18,440
You bastard!

120
00:11:40,840 --> 00:11:43,340
A battlefield is a sanctuary for men.

121
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:46,560
What outrageous conduct
would lead a woman here?

122
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:50,430
I, the leader of the Blue Whale
Super Strong Heavy Assault Knights...

123
00:11:50,430 --> 00:11:53,480
...Lord Adon, will teach
you a lesson for this!

124
00:11:56,690 --> 00:11:57,480
He's coming!

125
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:14,830
Big sister!

126
00:12:14,830 --> 00:12:16,460
Damn you!

127
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:18,460
Idiot!

128
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:19,250
Stay back!

129
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:27,640
W-What a fighter...

130
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:28,430
Casca!

131
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:30,310
Get back, Judeau!

132
00:12:30,310 --> 00:12:31,850
I'll find a way to kill him!

133
00:12:31,850 --> 00:12:36,310
So useless... No wonder
you are all under that woman's thumb.

134
00:12:36,310 --> 00:12:37,770
What was that?

135
00:12:52,660 --> 00:12:54,000
What will you do now?

136
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,500
There is no ground behind you.

137
00:12:59,170 --> 00:13:01,130
Hey, now, look at this.

138
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:06,640
Well, I see. You look rather pretty
even though you are dressed...

139
00:13:07,140 --> 00:13:09,180
...in the manner of a man.

140
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:12,220
Now, I will give you a chance.

141
00:13:14,270 --> 00:13:19,110
If you will be an obedient captive,
I will not kill you here.

142
00:13:19,110 --> 00:13:23,780
Being captive means you may serve
as my army's prostitute, of course.

143
00:13:24,950 --> 00:13:26,450
Son of a bitch...

144
00:13:26,450 --> 00:13:29,530
So, you call me a son of a bitch...

145
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:33,620
Then you will be buried by a bastard you hate!

146
00:13:33,870 --> 00:13:34,700
Big sister!

147
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:38,750
What?

148
00:13:45,510 --> 00:13:46,840
This is not like you.

149
00:13:47,380 --> 00:13:48,550
Guts...

150
00:13:49,510 --> 00:13:50,680
Commander!

151
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,560
Guts!

152
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:09,360
Come on.

153
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:13,910
I don't care who you are. I just want
to swing my sword against someone...

154
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:16,960
Until I'm so exhausted
that I can't think anymore!

155
00:14:17,410 --> 00:14:19,790
Enough with your stupid remarks!

156
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:34,220
Well done, I praise you for blocking my strike!

157
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:37,430
However, a fluke never happens twice!

158
00:14:43,270 --> 00:14:46,230
Can you defend against my special
strike that can even pulverize marble?

159
00:14:46,230 --> 00:14:47,610
This is the spearmanship...

160
00:14:47,610 --> 00:14:51,240
...that has been passed down through
the Coborlwitz family for 140 years.

161
00:14:52,990 --> 00:14:54,910
The ultimate secret technique...

162
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:58,040
Ganzansenpu...

163
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,260
Ganzansenpu?

164
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:18,060
What the hell?

165
00:15:21,230 --> 00:15:22,810
A-Amazing...

166
00:15:23,190 --> 00:15:25,320
He beat that monster with only two blows.

167
00:15:27,570 --> 00:15:28,990
Nothing less from our captain.

168
00:15:28,990 --> 00:15:30,150
Way to go!

169
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:38,160
What's wrong?

170
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:42,120
It's totally unlike you,
losing your edge in combat.

171
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:44,250
Get it together or you'll get killed.

172
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:50,220
H-Hey!

173
00:16:04,650 --> 00:16:05,770
Guts!

174
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,200
Guts!

175
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,660
Casca!

176
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:11,380
Never again...

177
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:13,170
I'll never go in the water with my armor.

178
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,810
Shit.

179
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:32,500
She's got a serious fever. 
It looks bad.

180
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:03,320
If I make a fire, the enemy
might spot it and find us.

181
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,500
Damn it!

182
00:19:12,500 --> 00:19:14,130
I guess there's no other way.

183
00:19:18,210 --> 00:19:22,590
We did this sort of thing once.
It's no big deal!

184
00:19:22,970 --> 00:19:28,060
What the hell? With that fever of
hers, she thinks she can still fight?

185
00:19:48,870 --> 00:19:50,580
So that's it.

186
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:59,670
It's pretty tough to be a woman...

187
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:07,560
Guts and Casca...

188
00:20:08,010 --> 00:20:12,060
The cliff was quite high, but a river
ran below it, so they must have...

189
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:17,320
You know how Guts is.
They're probably alive, but...

190
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:19,980
I couldn't see if they
landed safely from that fall.

191
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:22,240
And the captain was already
injured in the battle...

192
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:24,950
Casca was not quite herself as well.

193
00:20:24,950 --> 00:20:28,280
We should get a search party
out there right away.

194
00:20:29,620 --> 00:20:32,250
Lord Griffith, you must understand this...

195
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:37,040
In a battle, our utmost concern
is to conquer the enemy.

196
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:41,460
It is outrageous to use soldiers who
have been gifted to you by the king...

197
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:44,590
...to search during a battle
to ensure the safety of a mere...

198
00:20:44,590 --> 00:20:45,970
...troop commander.

199
00:20:46,390 --> 00:20:51,350
Besides, this happened because
they recklessly entered single combat.

200
00:20:51,770 --> 00:20:53,640
No, that's not true...

201
00:20:57,650 --> 00:21:02,150
The Raiders' leader and the famous
female company commander...

202
00:21:02,150 --> 00:21:05,150
The two most skilled commanders
are together, aren't they?

203
00:21:05,490 --> 00:21:09,580
Supposedly, they are able
to take such troubles in stride.

204
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:14,790
Indeed, I suppose
they will if they are still alive.

205
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

206
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

207
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

208
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

209
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

210
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

211
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

212
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

213
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

214
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

215
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

